Package: GameOptimizer
Title: A package for analyzing and optimizing video game performance and strategies
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: "James Angeles <jangeles@usf.edu> [aut, cre]"
Description: This package provides tools for analyzing and optimizing strategies 
    in video games, focusing on performance improvement, resource management, 
    and decision-making. It offers utilities for visualizing player statistics, 
    simulating different strategies, and analyzing gameplay to identify areas for 
    improvement. GameOptimizer is designed for competitive players, game developers, 
    and analysts to enhance gaming performance and experience.
Depends: R (>= 3.1.2)
Imports: dplyr, ggplot2, data.table, tidyr
License: MIT
LazyData: true
